Scope of this repository
------------------------
The original package was imported from the shipped archive, including
the import fixes it carries (if __package__:
dual-mode imports, and the persistent sparse top-k megakernel exposed under
both persistent_moa_norm_sparse_topk_megakernel and
persistent_norm_sparse_topk_agg_kernel in every environment).

Stage I.D adapts the project-supplied standalone Viral Nucleic Acid Invasion
Operator for the required molecular modulation in the unified architecture.
The operator code, tests, documentation and visualization tooling are covered
by the LICENSE file below.

Upstream defects found and fixed here
-------------------------------------
Four Triton launch sites in the operator package passed argument names that do
not exist in the corresponding @triton.jit kernel signatures, so every GPU
(code path) forward pass raised TypeError. The NumPy path was unaffected, which
is why CPU-only testing never caught them. Fixed here (one line each):

  baryogenesis_parity_operators.py:516
      delta_mass=delta_mass      ->  delta_mass_sq=delta_mass ** 2
  neuro_nonlinear_operators.py:463
      fhn_kappa=fhn_kappa        ->  kappa_sq3=3.0 * (fhn_kappa ** 2)
  quantum_tidal_operators.py:481
      M_HARM=M                    ->  M_HARMONICS=M
  supermembrane_spacetime_operators.py:497
      tau_brane=..., beta_flux=... ->  tau_sq=tau_brane ** 2, beta_sq=beta_flux ** 2

The squared / cubed forms match the NumPy reference implementations in the same
files.

Two further launch sites passed one extra positional argument, so the value
landed on a constexpr slot that was also given by keyword:

  quantum_tidal_operators.py:480
      removed harm_phases.contiguous(),  (the Triton kernel has no HarmPhases slot)
  spinal_cord_pathway_operators.py:541
      removed the extra positional D,   (the kernel has no stride_row slot)

Note for upstream: the Triton kernel of quantum_tidal ignores the harmonic
phase offsets entirely (u_tidal += c_m * cos(m*omega*t), while the NumPy path
uses cos(m*omega*t + harm_phases[m-1])). This is harmless for the unified layer,
whose init_layer_parameters sets harm_phases to zeros, but the two paths would
diverge if non-zero phases were ever supplied. viz/check_gpu_launch.py now runs all 14 domain operators forward+backward
on CUDA and cross-checks each against the CPU path, so this class of defect is
caught automatically from now on.

